 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Source-registered (S81-SLICE ring stop + x streamer): every data input lands in a flop at the pin (rstop iw / ie / iv / xf_q / xfv_q / neo_q / nwo_q / ci_q / cid_q / sid_c; xs isv_q / isd_q) and every output leaves a flop (rstop ro_e / ro_w / vo / nx regs / dl_* regs; xs xw_d relay register, xw_v = its bit 0; xg fault register). recipe-3 pin_regs would add a second unpriced stage per ring hop (SPEC: +1 ring-stop register ~ +8 cycles per ring traversal) and break the landed-slice lockstep (C1 / C3) latencies. pin_reg_split clones shared output launch flops; io_flop_at_pins anchors every pin flop at its face."
 },
 "reset_landing": {
  "enable": true,
  "stages": 2
 },
 "io_flop_at_pins": {
  "cols": 4,
  "allow_none": true
 },
 "keep_pin_regs": true,
 "pin_reg_split": true,
 "pre_cts_extra": [
  "physical/common_flow/clock_split_km.tcl"
 ],
 "orfs_vars": {
  "OT_CKKM_K": "16"
 },
 "fill_reason": {
  "pin_bound": "Pin-bound: 11,914 signal pins (W 2,554 ring W + NX W, E 2,554, N 3,762 control-plane deliveries / inject / issuer word, S 3,047 own fragments + V rung + frame word); 648 x 561.6 keeps every face <= 5.8 pins/um (N 5.8, S 4.7, W/E 4.5). 31 macros (24 SRAM 128x256 x buffer, 7 ROM 4096x72) ~ 112k um2."
 },
 "structural_change": "S81-XG successor (LEAD2-S81/SLICE 10-19, after s81sl_xg gate2 GRT stalled 4 h in congestion at 12 % std util): rstop RELAY=1 (every rstop output leaves through a relay register: no single-cycle wire across the 648-um tile; line/V payload reset-free, valid bits reset only) + xs RD2=1 (24-macro read crossbar -> bank-local 8:1 registered beside each bank column + 3:1 bank stage; long read wires 24x1536 -> 3x1536). +1 edge on rstop outputs, +1 on xw_d. Prior: S81-XG (10-19): new hardened gather sub-leaf of the S81 slice centre (C1 / C3 master child u_xg, 16 per die): ring stop data plane ot_s81sl_rstop (tier line E/W 1,104 b, V rung 276 b, NX snake ends, sid = 2*col + tier decode from S81-LBGAP G2 1b7c4b828) + x streamer ot_s81sl_xs (kit s81sl_xs floorplan v2 of 1dcaa1b20, never routed). The rstop -> xs gather port (3 x 1,031 b a cycle) stays internal. Floorplan: per-source x-buffer bank columns facing their ring faces (bank 1 = from W at x 86.4, bank 0 = own / V at 216, bank 2 = from E at 432), the 7 ROMs abutted in one column at 345.6 between bank 0 and bank 2 (calendar / phase / stream control in the middle), std-cell ring around the macros for the face pin-flop bands; clock + reset at the S-face centre. Same RTL cycles as the slice benches; reset landed at the face (2 stages, ROOT-RST). Gate1 (10-19, ot-agidock128) died at macro placement: the ROOT-RST landing-only wrapper (pin_regs off + reset_landing on) renames the core u_ot_pr_core, so the spec's u_s.* instance names matched nothing -> instance patterns are globs '*u_s.g_bank?b?.g_mac?m?.u_mem' / '*u_s.u_<rom>' (match with or without the wrapper).",
